{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** A v7 control that returns `{}` still lets the probe pass. I reproduced this through the real response parser with a stubbed provider.\n\n1. **Require readable control content.** Any non-null JSON currently counts as received. `{}` and `[]` both passed the completeness check, and a JSON string crashed packet generation. Require the fields readers need, while keeping readable v7 answers refused by the request-time check. [Answer handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:38)\n2. **Reject contradictory readings before counting them.** Three `8807` readings marked `omitted` with `valid_support: true` produced **pass**. An incomplete Part C comparison marked `read: false` still produced **not ready** from its claimed harm. Validate that each reading belongs to a planned, readable answer or completed comparison, and that its values agree. [Reading validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:43)\n3. **Keep the complete source text in the packets.** The 600-character cutoff removes the final $390–395B estimate from the `v14` dependency text shown to `linked-1:8834`. The packet also drops the answer’s explanation of what changed. Both are available in the saved input and answer. [Packet generation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_read.py:123)\n4. **Compare the bytes the transport actually sends.** The updated stub catches property reordering, but it uses `ensure_ascii=False` while the live transport escapes non-ASCII characters. I verified that the two produce different bytes for `linked-1:8834`. Capture the serialized HTTP body with the network call stubbed and compare it to the independently built expectation. [Rehearsal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_rehearsal.py:51) · [Live serialization](/Users/lchingen/hive